IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `la-dates`
IMPORT `la-rules`
IMPORT `la-seat`

-- Limitation Act 2005 (WA) -- worked cases for the claimant's questions (la-seat.l4), the date helpers (la-dates.l4) and
-- the regulative rule (la-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from
-- the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are
-- illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`no date` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000
`PI` MEANS `damages for a personal injury`
`FAA` MEANS `a Fatal Accidents Act 1959 action for a death`
`other` MEANS `any other cause of action`
`deed` MEANS `an action on a deed`

-- An adult with no extension facts: born 1 January 1980.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`, `accrued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`adult limit` k `accrued` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k FALSE FALSE `accrued` (`d` 1 1 1980) FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `no date`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`, `accrued` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`adult can commence` k `accrued` `the day` MEANS
    `Can I still commence my action on this day` k FALSE FALSE `accrued` (`d` 1 1 1980) FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `no date` `the day`

-- A claimant under 18 at accrual: days without a guardian, close relationship.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`, `accrued` IS A DATE, `born` IS A DATE, `no guardian days` IS A NUMBER, `close` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`minor limit` k `accrued` `born` `no guardian days` `close` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k FALSE FALSE `accrued` `born` FALSE `no guardian days` `close` FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `no date`

-- An adult (born 1 January 1980) with a mental disability since accrual.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`, `accrued` IS A DATE, `no guardian days` IS A NUMBER, `close` IS A BOOLEAN, `ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `ended on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`disabled limit` k `accrued` `no guardian days` `close` `ended` `ended on` MEANS
    `By when must I commence my action` k FALSE FALSE `accrued` (`d` 1 1 1980) FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE `no guardian days` `close` `ended` `ended on`

GIVEN `y` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`last day` `y` MEANS `the last day to commence is` `y`

§§ `Dates`

-- 3 years from 10 March 2020 end with 10 March 2023; 6 years from 29 February 2020 end with 28 February 2026 (fork F1);
-- 4 years from 29 February 2020 end with 29 February 2024; 100 days after 1 June 2021 is 9 September 2021 (29 + 31 + 31
-- + 9); the day before 1 January 2027 is 31 December 2026.
#ASSERT `the anniversary` 3 `years after` (`d` 10 3 2020) EQUALS `d` 10 3 2023
#ASSERT `the anniversary` 6 `years after` (`d` 29 2 2020) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the anniversary` 4 `years after` (`d` 29 2 2020) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `the date` 100 `days after` (`d` 1 6 2021) EQUALS `d` 9 9 2021
#ASSERT `the day before` (`d` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 31 12 2026
#ASSERT `the day of reaching age` 21 `for birth on` (`d` 1 6 2005) EQUALS `d` 1 6 2026

§§ `ss 55-57 -- when a personal injury claim accrued`

-- Arguments: dust, aware, day aware, first sign, day of sign, knew before 1984, knowledge, day of knowledge, died, day of death.
-- s 55: the earlier of awareness (10 March 2020) and the first sign (1 February 2020).
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 2 2020) FALSE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` EQUALS `it accrued on` (`d` 1 2 2020)
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2020) FALSE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` EQUALS `it accrued on` (`d` 10 3 2020)
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2020) FALSE `no date` FALSE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` EQUALS `it accrued on` (`d` 10 3 2020)
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` FALSE FALSE `no date` TRUE (`d` 7 7 2021) FALSE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` EQUALS `it accrued on` (`d` 7 7 2021)
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` FALSE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` FALSE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` EQUALS `it has not yet accrued`
-- s 57(1): no accrual before the death, so at the death; a sign recorded after the death does not count.
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` FALSE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` FALSE FALSE `no date` TRUE (`d` 5 5 2021) EQUALS `it accrued on` (`d` 5 5 2021)
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` FALSE FALSE `no date` TRUE (`d` 1 6 2021) FALSE FALSE `no date` TRUE (`d` 5 5 2021) EQUALS `it accrued on` (`d` 5 5 2021)
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` FALSE FALSE `no date` TRUE (`d` 1 4 2021) FALSE FALSE `no date` TRUE (`d` 5 5 2021) EQUALS `it accrued on` (`d` 1 4 2021)
-- s 56(1): dust; knowledge before 1984 takes the case outside both s 55 and s 56.
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` TRUE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 1983) FALSE `no date` EQUALS `this Act does not say when it accrued`
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` TRUE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 8 2022) FALSE `no date` EQUALS `it accrued on` (`d` 1 8 2022)
-- For dust, awareness and first signs are not the test (s 55(2)): knowledge on 1 August 2022 still decides.
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2015) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2014) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 8 2022) FALSE `no date` EQUALS `it accrued on` (`d` 1 8 2022)
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` TRUE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` FALSE FALSE `no date` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2023) EQUALS `it accrued on` (`d` 3 3 2023)
#ASSERT `When did my personal injury claim accrue` TRUE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` FALSE FALSE `no date` FALSE `no date` EQUALS `it has not yet accrued`

